# MC 10062.30.1 applied to the two generated-output families still slipping the rule (orchestrator 10252.1, 2026-10-07):
# quality-gate records and root-level gate screenshots stay on disk, untracked (they are run records, never product)
**/QUALITY.md
/[0-9][0-9]-*.png

/salong-*.png

# root-level *.png = transient browser-QA staging for ALL lanes (owner ruling MC 10062.30.1 precedent, generalized 2026-10-08: zero tracked root PNGs ever; product images live under projects/). Run owners still relocate their own shots to their run dirs.
/*.png

# MC 11003 follow-up (owner ruling 2026-10-22: "rec on all and fix the np/, projects/np trap. doctrine is /projects/np"; DA gate P2-A/P1-A): NO ignore rule here guards the root `<site>/` browse surface. The `/*/index.html` wildcard this line replaces was measured path by path: it also swallowed docs/index.html, tools/index.html, out/index.html and every future site dir, caught nothing at depth 2, and its only effect beyond the writer's own refusal was to make a stray INVISIBLE to git status — the visibility that found the trap in the first place. One mechanism per concern: tools/build-index.py's build_root() REFUSAL without --host-surface is the enforcement, and tools/test_build_index.py asserts that every page build_root() writes is committable by a plain `git add`. A root `<site>/index.html` is a GENERATED MIRROR, never source: projects/<site>/ is canon.
# NOT a wildcard and NOT about generated output (that is the line above's concern): the wedding privacy marker is machine-local guard state that must stay on disk untracked — a tracked projects/wedding/ path makes EVERY later push of main DENIED by .git/hooks/pre-push.local (measured: push rc=1, control rc=0), so this exact root-anchored path is ignored to keep a stray `git add` from deadlocking the repo's push path. The guard is armed BY THE FILE ON DISK, not by tracking; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §8.8 states the protection in force.
/projects/wedding/LOCAL_ONLY
# MC 11796 wedding-40 run (2026-10-31): the wedding privacy boundary (§8.8, owner ruling 2026-10-12) named as ONE root-anchored path: NO byte under projects/wedding/ may ever be committed — .git/hooks/pre-push.local poisons the repo's WHOLE push path if wedding bytes enter history (measured: push rc=1). The invisibility here is the INTENDED inverse of §8 item 9's wildcard ban: that ban forbids a wildcard hiding generated output from the tidiness check; this names ONE real directory whose every byte is uncommittable by privacy ruling, so a stray `git add -A` can never recreate the push deadlock (same reasoning as the LOCAL_ONLY line above, widened to the whole dir this run fills). It UNTRACKS nothing: `git ls-files projects/wedding` is empty (measured 2026-10-31). Caveat shared with LOCAL_ONLY: `git clean -fdX` removes wedding content too — it lives nowhere else (LOCAL-ONLY).
/projects/wedding/
